course: dictionary
lesson: 3457
title: Fahrenheit, a temperature scale
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fahrenheit is a scale for measuring temperature, which tells us how hot or cold something is. A thermometer with a Fahrenheit scale shows the heat in degrees. The small ° sign after a number, as in 98.6 °F, means degrees Fahrenheit.
explain: Fahrenheit is also a name. The scale is named after the scientist Daniel Gabriel Fahrenheit, who invented it. «Fahrenheit is named after Daniel Gabriel Fahrenheit, a German-speaking scientist.» That is why the word begins with a capital F.
explain: On this scale, water freezes at 32 degrees and boils at 212 degrees. Context helps you decide which scale is being used. A weather report or oven in the USA is likely to use Fahrenheit, but in the UK most temperatures are in Celsius.
fact: Fahrenheit is a scale for measuring temperature.
fact: Water freezes at 32 degrees Fahrenheit and boils at 212 degrees Fahrenheit.
fact: Fahrenheit is named after the scientist Daniel Gabriel Fahrenheit, who invented the scale.
fact: Normal body temperature is 98.6 °F.
fact: Fahrenheit is spelled F-A-H-R-E-N-H-E-I-T, with "ei" as in German.
exercise: What is Fahrenheit, as a scale? | A type of ruler for measuring length | A unit for weighing things | *A scale for measuring temperature | A kind of cooking pot
exercise: At what Fahrenheit temperature does water freeze? | *32 | 100 | 0 | 212
exercise: «Fahrenheit is named after Daniel Gabriel Fahrenheit, a German-speaking scientist.» Why does the word begin with a capital F? | It means very hot | *It is a name, taken from a person | It is a very long word | It is always written in capitals, even in the middle of a sentence
test: What temperature is normal for the human body on the Fahrenheit scale? | 32 | 212 | *98.6 | 100
test: Which country uses Fahrenheit most often for weather reports? | New Zealand | Ireland | Australia | *USA
exam: On which scale does water boil at 212 degrees? | Kelvin metres | Celsius | *Fahrenheit
